## Authentication
Session Token (x-xsrftoken) — Authentication method detected from captured traffic.

### Providing credentials
- Prefer passing auth as request headers or cookies at call time (do not hardcode secrets into the skill).
- If executing via an external proxy/executor, pass per-call credentials (cookies and/or headers) so they are not persisted.

## Dependencies
- Runtime capable of HTTPS requests.
- If using `scripts/api.ts`: TypeScript toolchain (or transpile to JS).

## Endpoints

### Auth Flow (2)
- `GET /api/v3/oauth/captcha/v2` — Retrieve a CAPTCHA for OAuth authentication.
- `GET /api/v3/oauth/sms/supported_countries` — Get supported countries for SMS authentication.

### Data Read (1)
- `GET /api/v1/captcha/js` — Retrieve JavaScript code for CAPTCHA handling.

### Data Write (1)
- `POST /{id}` — Post data associated with a specific ID.

### Search (1)
- `GET /search` — Perform a search query on the platform.

### Realtime (1)
- `POST /zbst/events/r` — Send real-time event data to the server.

### Config (1)
- `GET /api/v2/getconf` — Fetch configuration settings for the application.

## Quick Start

### OpenClaw (Unbrowse) workflow
- Authenticate in the browser first (no credentials are shipped with this skill).
- Capture fresh auth locally: run `unbrowse_capture` on an authenticated page for this domain.
- Execute via backend gate + client browser executor: `unbrowse_replay` with `executionMode="backend"`.

Example:
```text
unbrowse_replay { service: "zhihu", executionMode: "backend", endpoint: "GET /api/v1/captcha/js" }
```

